title: More XCM rollback hardening
doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |-
      Adding more hardening to the XCM executor. None of the fixes are vulnerabilities, but _could become_
      so later if executor upstream or downstream assumptions change.
      This PR reduces the number of assumptions by adding defense in depth directly on the executor,
      and adds documentation and tests for remaining assumptions.
      Changes:
      1. roll back delivery fees of report instructions and failed BuyExecution state
      2. Harden `BuyExecution` by recording the asset to be used for delivery fees only when BuyExecution succeeds.
      3. fail ExportMessage when the exporter cannot deliver
      4. run the remaining storage-mutating instructions transactionally
      5. document the invariants behind register rollback
crates:
  - name: staging-xcm-executor
    bump: patch
  - name: pallet-xcm
    bump: none
